00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:04.033
And I got to know,

00:42:05.000 --> 00:42:07.650
these are not the people
you see on college campuses

00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:09.240
or you see on Twitter, right?

00:42:09.240 --> 00:42:11.940
These are, they can be
progressive on some others,

00:42:11.940 --> 00:42:14.280
on some things, and
conservative in others.

00:42:14.280 --> 00:42:17.120
And there have been this type of mix.

00:42:17.120 --> 00:42:19.260
Not the ideologues from one side.

00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:21.710
This kind of mix have
been our biggest allies

00:42:21.710 --> 00:42:24.470
for the organization, and
for me, as an individual,

00:42:24.470 --> 00:42:27.430
but also as an organization,
so I think it's that,

00:42:27.430 --> 00:42:29.610
that, I think there's
also study done on Twitter

00:42:29.610 --> 00:42:32.390
is that how, like those
who are actually on Twitter

00:42:32.390 --> 00:42:34.370
are those crazy maniacs.

00:42:34.370 --> 00:42:36.813
It's kind of a self
selection, is that this is,

00:42:38.200 --> 00:42:42.230
like even I had a lot of
prejudices against the right,

00:42:42.230 --> 00:42:43.281
when I moved to the United States.

00:42:43.281 --> 00:42:45.790
- [Dave] That's exactly
what I was gonna say.

00:42:45.790 --> 00:42:47.310
- And when I,

00:42:47.310 --> 00:42:52.310
and obviously hearing the
left wing or that section,

00:42:52.630 --> 00:42:54.840
the talk show host, and
to have made a boogeyman

00:42:54.840 --> 00:42:56.700
of these people.

00:42:56.700 --> 00:42:59.740
And other than the actual boogeymen

00:42:59.740 --> 00:43:02.160
and those who are also talk
show hosts of the right wing

00:43:02.160 --> 00:43:04.490
establishment, but most
people who are conservative

00:43:04.490 --> 00:43:06.460
are also very nice people, you know?

00:43:06.460 --> 00:43:08.130
So I think it's that that is,

00:43:08.130 --> 00:43:12.110
the problem is that how can
we give these guys platform?

00:43:12.110 --> 00:43:14.020
Which I think you are doing some of.

00:43:14.020 --> 00:43:15.950
I think it's that--

00:43:15.950 --> 00:43:17.590
- Wait, who do you mean, these guys?

00:43:17.590 --> 00:43:19.530
- Those who are actually sane people,

00:43:19.530 --> 00:43:21.350
who are not fighting with--

00:43:21.350 --> 00:43:22.210
- I'm trying, man!

00:43:22.210 --> 00:43:25.990
- Yeah, who are not like,
starting at Dave Rubin,

00:43:25.990 --> 00:43:27.040
blah, blah, blah, blah, blah, or like,

00:43:27.040 --> 00:43:28.320
at Faisal, like you know?

00:43:28.320 --> 00:43:32.200
These are, unfortunately
they are very the loudest

00:43:32.200 --> 00:43:34.421
in most of the, but,

00:43:34.421 --> 00:43:37.490
I'm now realizing it after
I said I quit the news

00:43:37.490 --> 00:43:38.420
and even social media,

00:43:38.420 --> 00:43:41.083
I only post selfies of me eating shawarma.

00:43:42.300 --> 00:43:47.300
But I think it's that as I
go outside, and I am now,

00:43:47.610 --> 00:43:49.980
and then yeah, many people
are actually really nice.

00:43:49.980 --> 00:43:51.620
- It's interesting because, you know,

00:43:51.620 --> 00:43:53.870
I've traveled the country,
and the world actually,

00:43:53.870 --> 00:43:56.290
about 20 countries over
the course of last year,

00:43:56.290 --> 00:43:57.360
on tour with Jordan.

00:43:57.360 --> 00:43:59.763
And that also, my main takeaway was that.

00:44:00.721 --> 00:44:03.540
It is particularly unique
here in the United States,

00:44:03.540 --> 00:44:06.030
how great everyone is.

00:44:06.030 --> 00:44:06.863
- [Faisal] It's amazing.

00:44:06.863 --> 00:44:08.280
- Okay, so now, as a citizen here,

00:44:08.280 --> 00:44:10.000
somebody that's been
here for six plus years.

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:10.833
- [Faisal] Yeah.

00:44:10.833 --> 00:44:11.666
Proudly so.

00:44:11.666 --> 00:44:14.380
- How often do you face
hate and face racism?

00:44:14.380 --> 00:44:16.510
Let's say from the quarters
that they would tell you

00:44:16.510 --> 00:44:18.350
you're supposed to getting it from?

00:44:18.350 --> 00:44:20.270
Are the Trump supporters hunting you down?

00:44:20.270 --> 00:44:23.020
- I mean, thank goodness,
not that I know of.

00:44:23.020 --> 00:44:24.687
But no, I mean, I think--

00:44:24.687 --> 00:44:26.617
- But I mean, we go out
all the time in New York,

00:44:26.617 --> 00:44:29.145
and you make all sorts
of funny Arabic jokes

00:44:29.145 --> 00:44:30.720
to the waiters and waitresses.

00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:32.200
- You're by the way,
the only person I know

00:44:32.200 --> 00:44:34.110
that when you sit down at a restaurant,

00:44:34.110 --> 00:44:35.990
you order two drinks at once.

00:44:35.990 --> 00:44:37.540
- I get a glass of red wine.

00:44:37.540 --> 00:44:39.886
You get a beer and a margarita.

00:44:39.886 --> 00:44:41.680
- Because I know I'm gonna order them,

00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:44.090
so might as well get them
together, so that way--

00:44:44.090 --> 00:44:45.650
- But then the margarita
just starts melting.

00:44:45.650 --> 00:44:47.250
I've tried to explain this to you.

00:44:47.250 --> 00:44:49.520
- My physics knowledge is very limited.

00:44:49.520 --> 00:44:51.493
But, yeah.

00:44:52.752 --> 00:44:53.585
I mean--

00:44:53.585 --> 00:44:55.632
- But really, do you face any racism

00:44:55.632 --> 00:44:59.050
that you know of in America,
any anti immigrant feeling?

00:44:59.050 --> 00:45:01.083
- So yes and no.

00:45:02.068 --> 00:45:04.850
I mean you invited me to be on your show

00:45:04.850 --> 00:45:05.683
when the travel ban happened,

00:45:05.683 --> 00:45:07.840
and my mom was in Iraq when that,

00:45:07.840 --> 00:45:10.693
so that thing affected
actually me personally.

00:45:11.900 --> 00:45:15.810
Overall, I mean yes, I think
it being any public figure

00:45:15.810 --> 00:45:19.730
of any sort, you get,
hate is part of the game.

00:45:19.730 --> 00:45:22.313
But it's much significantly less.

00:45:22.313 --> 00:45:23.146
- [Dave] But I mean, just in day to day--

00:45:23.146 --> 00:45:24.990
is in no way comparison, like,

00:45:24.990 --> 00:45:26.884
like, I mean maybe my sandals are low.

00:45:26.884 --> 00:45:27.717
- I don't mean hate though, I mean,

00:45:27.717 --> 00:45:29.820
I don't mean hate like,
I don't like his policy,

00:45:29.820 --> 00:45:31.060
I don't like him, something like that.

00:45:31.060 --> 00:45:33.300
I mean that you are a brown
immigrant in the United States.

00:45:33.300 --> 00:45:34.133
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:45:34.133 --> 00:45:36.930
No, I mean overall I
would say, yeah, I mean,

00:45:36.930 --> 00:45:40.060
by any comparison, like compared to living

00:45:40.060 --> 00:45:43.290
in the Middle East to here, is in no way.

00:45:43.290 --> 00:45:45.130
I mean not even, I mean,

00:45:45.130 --> 00:45:48.300
I mean I think there are...

00:45:48.300 --> 00:45:51.020
Obviously some people have
different definitions, but,

00:45:51.020 --> 00:45:53.730
I think, is it dehabilitating to my life?

00:45:53.730 --> 00:45:54.563
No.

00:45:55.620 --> 00:45:58.040
Having, I think by most
accounts, a good life.

00:45:58.040 --> 00:45:59.870
I love living in America.

00:45:59.870 --> 00:46:00.910
I love my friends here.

00:46:00.910 --> 00:46:05.020
I think that, I now have a
strong bond to this country

00:46:05.020 --> 00:46:07.560
as a country who accepted
me from the environment

00:46:07.560 --> 00:46:10.730
that I still live in,
and really gave me that,

00:46:10.730 --> 00:46:13.450
I think the American dream,
I think I'm a symbol of it

00:46:13.450 --> 00:46:14.283
in a way.

00:46:14.283 --> 00:46:15.210
- Well that's what I love.

00:46:15.210 --> 00:46:17.097
Seeing your posts, I love
seeing you on Instagram,

00:46:17.097 --> 00:46:19.080
and you've, you know, when
you just posted all this stuff

00:46:19.080 --> 00:46:21.320
from the party that you had when you

00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:23.190
officially became a citizen,
you got the big American hat

00:46:23.190 --> 00:46:24.410
on, the American jersey.

00:46:24.410 --> 00:46:26.960
And it's like, you are
the American dream to me.

00:46:26.960 --> 00:46:27.943
I really believe that.

00:46:27.943 --> 00:46:30.500
- And the people who attended
that party, by the way,

00:46:30.500 --> 00:46:32.210
I had a party to be a US citizen,

00:46:32.210 --> 00:46:33.620
and the people who came to the party

00:46:33.620 --> 00:46:35.810
are from every faction, of,

00:46:35.810 --> 00:46:38.610
of either humanity or political views.

00:46:38.610 --> 00:46:43.370
And, no, I think it's that those who can

00:46:43.370 --> 00:46:46.770
always look for fights will
find them, as in any case,

00:46:46.770 --> 00:46:47.797
but I think it's that,

00:46:47.797 --> 00:46:50.070
and obviously everyone's
experience is different.

00:46:50.070 --> 00:46:53.650
I mean I don't live in,
I don't know, small town,

00:46:53.650 --> 00:46:54.950
I don't live in the Bronx.

00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:58.480
These people might have
different experiences than I do.

00:46:58.480 --> 00:47:02.070
But I think, I mean, I would
be dishonest to play this

00:47:02.070 --> 00:47:05.030
identity politics, oh, I'm a
victim here, and I think life--

00:47:05.030 --> 00:47:06.357
- I've done events with you in Texas

00:47:06.357 --> 00:47:08.481
and then we've gone to local bars,

00:47:08.481 --> 00:47:10.260
where redneck bars, remember that night?

00:47:10.260 --> 00:47:11.850
I forget what town we were in.

00:47:11.850 --> 00:47:14.150
But we went to that,
what the average person

00:47:14.150 --> 00:47:17.080
would think is some middle
America redneck bar,

00:47:17.080 --> 00:47:19.220
and we had a great freaking
time and nobody cared,

00:47:19.220 --> 00:47:21.830
and you're loud, right, you're
always loud and laughing,

00:47:21.830 --> 00:47:23.330
and nobody cares.

00:47:23.330 --> 00:47:26.850
- No, yeah, I think these are a lot of

00:47:28.380 --> 00:47:31.660
polarizing misconceptions
that need to be fought.

00:47:31.660 --> 00:47:34.010
I mean my parents live
in Texas, by the way.

00:47:34.010 --> 00:47:35.213
All my exes live in Texas.

00:47:35.213 --> 00:47:36.980
(laughing)

00:47:36.980 --> 00:47:40.700
Actually they don't, they live
in California, but, but I,

00:47:40.700 --> 00:47:43.440
no, I mean my parents live
in Texas, I go to many,

00:47:43.440 --> 00:47:45.083
I go to Texas quite a lot.

00:47:47.600 --> 00:47:49.480
This misconception that people there

00:47:49.480 --> 00:47:52.380
are a bunch of racists and,

00:47:52.380 --> 00:47:54.200
I mean I've also been to like small town,

00:47:54.200 --> 00:47:56.370
there is an area called
Frittersburg, Texas,

00:47:56.370 --> 00:48:00.260
which has kind of German
wineries and beers and stuff.

00:48:00.260 --> 00:48:02.270
And many people there were like Texans,

00:48:02.270 --> 00:48:04.948
and they were not antagonistic whatsoever,

00:48:04.948 --> 00:48:06.593
they were like super friendly.

00:48:07.540 --> 00:48:08.620
- Can you talk a little bit about,

00:48:08.620 --> 00:48:09.640
'cause you've been traveling a lot lately.

00:48:09.640 --> 00:48:10.890
I know you were in Europe

00:48:10.890 --> 00:48:12.980
just these last couple days actually.

00:48:12.980 --> 00:48:16.050
How the sort of integration
thing or race conversation

00:48:16.050 --> 00:48:17.730
or the rest of it, how
that's different here

00:48:17.730 --> 00:48:20.120
than it is in Europe,
from what you're finding?

00:48:20.120 --> 00:48:22.910
- I mean my, if there
is one word to describe,

00:48:22.910 --> 00:48:24.780
it's tense, man.

00:48:24.780 --> 00:48:26.288
It's tense.

00:48:26.288 --> 00:48:28.570
- So you were in Denmark,
you were in the UK.

00:48:28.570 --> 00:48:30.080
- I was in Denmark mostly.

00:48:30.080 --> 00:48:32.390
I was in Denmark for
like seven, eight days,

00:48:32.390 --> 00:48:35.673
and then I went to Norway
and I went to the UK.

00:48:36.510 --> 00:48:37.623
The thing is like,

00:48:38.480 --> 00:48:41.230
and also I've been to Germany and the UK.

00:48:41.230 --> 00:48:43.483
So I'm using my American passport.

00:48:47.070 --> 00:48:48.720
When I get the passport, I was like,

00:48:48.720 --> 00:48:50.610
let me go to Canada to maybe test it.

00:48:50.610 --> 00:48:51.610
Does this really work?

00:48:51.610 --> 00:48:53.750
And I went to Montreal, I was like,

00:48:53.750 --> 00:48:55.240
oh, this shit actually works!

00:48:55.240 --> 00:48:56.877
And I was like, okay,
I can go to Europe noW.

00:48:56.877 --> 00:48:59.026
- And that's hilarious, you
just wanted to test it out

00:48:59.026 --> 00:49:00.460
in Canada, 'cause that's a little easier.

00:49:00.460 --> 00:49:02.410
- Because it's the closest country.

00:49:02.410 --> 00:49:03.340
- I love it.

00:49:03.340 --> 00:49:04.510
You become an American citizen,

00:49:04.510 --> 00:49:05.800
you get a sharp leather jacket

00:49:05.800 --> 00:49:07.008
and you immediately go to Europe.

00:49:07.008 --> 00:49:08.840
(laughing)

00:49:08.840 --> 00:49:10.470
- Living good, yeah.

00:49:10.470 --> 00:49:11.950
I think it's that,

00:49:11.950 --> 00:49:15.210
I mean obviously, I
think the main difference

00:49:15.210 --> 00:49:19.030
between the United
States and Europe is that

00:49:20.070 --> 00:49:21.830
everybody can be American.

00:49:21.830 --> 00:49:23.540
America is a land of immigrants.

00:49:23.540 --> 00:49:26.800
At the core of it is that the identity

00:49:26.800 --> 00:49:28.507
is attached to values.

00:49:28.507 --> 00:49:32.430
And I mean, when I became
a US citizen, it was,

00:49:32.430 --> 00:49:34.790
I mean the test is easy,
but it's like, okay,

00:49:34.790 --> 00:49:36.793
what does United States,
what are the Bill of Rights,

00:49:36.793 --> 00:49:38.650
freedom of speech, all of that.

00:49:38.650 --> 00:49:40.010
- You mean you didn't
have to pledge allegiance

00:49:40.010 --> 00:49:41.920
to white power or something like that?

00:49:41.920 --> 00:49:42.753
That was not on the test?

00:49:42.753 --> 00:49:44.180
- Not this time, no.

00:49:44.180 --> 00:49:46.080
But they said come back in five years.

00:49:47.214 --> 00:49:49.080
(laughs)

00:49:49.080 --> 00:49:53.470
I think it's that, so,
that mixture of like,

00:49:53.470 --> 00:49:55.920
that this is a state based upon values,

00:49:55.920 --> 00:49:57.000
I mean that's one of the reasons.

00:49:57.000 --> 00:49:59.740
I mean I was actually had possibilities,

00:49:59.740 --> 00:50:01.470
I mean I was rejected from
entering the United Kingdom,

00:50:01.470 --> 00:50:03.380
but I had possibilities of
entering different states

00:50:03.380 --> 00:50:04.630
in Europe to immigrate.

00:50:04.630 --> 00:50:07.570
Even though I was in that tough situation,

00:50:07.570 --> 00:50:10.430
which I would take it
regardless where it come.

00:50:10.430 --> 00:50:12.580
If I had the choice I
would choose America.

00:50:12.580 --> 00:50:14.280
And I would still choose it again.

00:50:14.280 --> 00:50:18.410
Is that this is a land
that is based on values.

00:50:18.410 --> 00:50:21.540
So, as a result, see, you and I,

00:50:21.540 --> 00:50:24.150
having a conversation, we
had a margarita together

00:50:24.150 --> 00:50:25.663
in multiple states.

00:50:27.030 --> 00:50:29.710
I think, yes, while this can happen

00:50:29.710 --> 00:50:33.509
in different European
states, is that Europe...

00:50:33.509 --> 00:50:36.090
Europe in a way like Asia,
is part of the old world.

00:50:36.090 --> 00:50:40.330
And there is history and
there are conflicts there

00:50:40.330 --> 00:50:43.660
that if you are an immigrant, it is used,

00:50:43.660 --> 00:50:45.450
I mean when I was in Denmark,

00:50:45.450 --> 00:50:47.363
it was obvious I was a foreigner.

00:50:48.270 --> 00:50:49.630
It was obvious I was a foreigner,

00:50:49.630 --> 00:50:53.220
because Denmark has a
king, it has a history,

00:50:53.220 --> 00:50:56.240
it has, in a way, specific
tribe that eventually

00:50:56.240 --> 00:50:58.997
became a state, as in the case of many.

00:50:58.997 --> 00:51:01.320
- Although they are
struggling a little bit less

00:51:01.320 --> 00:51:02.320
with the immigration issue

00:51:02.320 --> 00:51:03.850
than the other Scandinavian
countries, right?

00:51:03.850 --> 00:51:05.650
At least that was my take
when I was in Denmark.

00:51:05.650 --> 00:51:07.690
- I mean it depends who you ask.

00:51:07.690 --> 00:51:10.138
I mean and now I think that
all the social democrats

00:51:10.138 --> 00:51:12.460
are getting tough on immigration,

00:51:12.460 --> 00:51:15.133
to protect the welfare
state and some of that.

00:51:17.960 --> 00:51:21.360
So you have this kind of,

00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:23.130
I would say the threshold to integrate

00:51:23.130 --> 00:51:24.510
is more difficult than America.

00:51:24.510 --> 00:51:26.970
I think America is easy to integrate to.

00:51:26.970 --> 00:51:31.670
I think many people, it's
a melting pot, I mean,

00:51:31.670 --> 00:51:34.010
some guys like, oh you're
not American enough,

00:51:34.010 --> 00:51:37.410
well like, I was like, I
drink Bud Light, is that...

00:51:37.410 --> 00:51:38.243
No, is like--

00:51:38.243 --> 00:51:39.667
- Did someone really ever say that to you?

00:51:39.667 --> 00:51:41.430
'Cause that would get
to my question earlier.

00:51:41.430 --> 00:51:43.374
- The guy was, the guy from England.

00:51:43.374 --> 00:51:44.207
(laughs)

00:51:44.207 --> 00:51:45.040
- The guy was from England?

00:51:45.040 --> 00:51:47.669
- Yeah I was telling
him, I was telling him,

00:51:47.669 --> 00:51:49.800
he's like, oh, you're not American.

00:51:49.800 --> 00:51:54.030
I was like, I don't have
time for you, but...

00:51:54.030 --> 00:51:57.910
So I think it's that the threshold
to enter American society

00:51:57.910 --> 00:52:00.220
or to integrate to America is different.

00:52:00.220 --> 00:52:04.530
I think, so, there, it's
more difficult to integrate.

00:52:04.530 --> 00:52:06.620
By default it's more
difficult to integrate.

00:52:06.620 --> 00:52:08.620
Imagine you're from Aleppo,

00:52:08.620 --> 00:52:11.570
and you grew up in a
religious Muslim background,

00:52:11.570 --> 00:52:16.570
in which you were taught
that the West is an enemy,

00:52:17.030 --> 00:52:20.480
or your values are more
superior to their values.

00:52:20.480 --> 00:52:22.200
Clash immediately happens.

00:52:22.200 --> 00:52:24.360
Is that like, it's already,

00:52:24.360 --> 00:52:27.080
I mean the Poles are difficult
to integrate in Denmark,

00:52:27.080 --> 00:52:32.080
leave aside somebody from
Raqqah, or small town Syria.

00:52:34.235 --> 00:52:37.090
So as a result, it is,

00:52:37.090 --> 00:52:41.760
so you have this state
with, to some extent,

00:52:41.760 --> 00:52:44.440
strong identity that
is tied to the history

00:52:44.440 --> 00:52:48.640
and tied to, in some
extent, ethnic identity,

00:52:48.640 --> 00:52:50.487
which I'm not a fan of, but these are,

00:52:50.487 --> 00:52:52.350
it's a different history.

00:52:52.350 --> 00:52:56.420
And then, it is not easy to,

00:52:56.420 --> 00:52:58.010
even if you are like, let's say,

00:52:58.010 --> 00:52:59.900
even if you are the secular open minded,

00:52:59.900 --> 00:53:02.030
